<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (Furrever Pals was built in HTML, CSS, and JavaScript, deliberately, not by default. HTML and CSS were the first languages I learned, and returning to them here felt right for a five page brand site with no complex state to manage. )
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
350 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 175 0 R
/E (The separation between structure, style, and behaviour keeps the codebase organized in a way that mirrors how I think about design systems: each layer doing one job clearly, rather than blending concerns the way a framework often does. Where interaction needed real logic, plain JavaScript handled it directly, DOM manipulation through querySelectorAll and classList rather than a library managing state on my behalf.)
/Pg 24 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
