<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Some of the site's interactions are simple by design. The FAQ accordion closes every open item before opening the one clicked, so only one answer shows at a time, a small rule that keeps the page from feeling cluttered as people click through.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
356 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 176 0 R
/E (Other pieces needed more thought. The reviews carousel had to work differently on mobile and desktop, showing one card at a time on a phone screen versus three side by side on desktop, so I built it to recalculate its own layout on load and on resize rather than relying on a fixed breakpoint that would eventually break. The hero carousel auto advances every four seconds, but if someone navigates manually, the timer resets so the next automatic slide does not feel like it is fighting the person's own input.)
/Pg 25 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
